    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-cpy-to-pcc-path-args",
      "delta": "ON multi 3683\u21923637 (-46), ON per-module sum 9906\u21929868 (-38), pipeline.py 1173\u21921119 (-54), layer1.py 5976\u21925992 (+16).",
      "reason": "Add a scoped CPython\u2192pcc object bridge for native os.path/os.access path arguments so CPython-backed path values no longer force os.path.join and related helpers back through py_cpy_* dispatch."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-list-literal-bridge",
      "delta": "ON multi 3637\u21923601 (-36), ON per-module sum 9868\u21929798 (-70), OFF total drops too \u2014 layer1.py OFF 23467\u219221474 (-1993), runtime_abi.py 6253\u21925535 (-718), class_gen 1349\u21921234 (-115), pipeline 1173\u21921110 (-63), marshal 358\u2192328 (-30).",
      "reason": "Extend the cpy\u2192pcc bridge from os.path arg sites to list literal element sites. When a list literal contains any CPython value, the previous code routed the entire list construction through _emit_cpython_list_ops (CPython-managed). With py_cpy_to_pcc_obj available (added by codex), each cpy element is bridged individually and the list stays pcc-native, breaking the chain-of-cpython amplifier at literal sites. cpy splat-extend stays on the cpython path because eagerly bridging the iterable would copy out elements that the splat-extend semantics doesn't promise."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-tuple-dict-literal-bridge",
      "delta": "OFF multi 27853\u219220416 (-7437), ON multi 3601\u21923454 (-147), ON per-module sum 9798\u21928397 (-1401). Largest OFF per-module drops: runtime_abi.py 5535\u21921152 (-4383), layer1.py 21474\u219220164 (-1310), type_infer.py 863\u2192658 (-205), pipeline.py 1110\u2192922 (-188).",
      "reason": "Extend the cpy\u2192pcc bridge from list literal element sites to tuple literal element sites and dict literal value sites, and add native py_tuple_concat so tuple + tuple-shaped Dyn no longer goes through CPython tuple.__add__. CPython-backed dict keys still use the CPython dict path so recursive marshalling does not change key identity/hash semantics; CPython splat iterables still use the legacy CPython list/tuple ops path."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-membership-set-dict-methods",
      "delta": "OFF multi 20416\u219219763 (-653), ON multi 3454\u21922695 (-759), ON per-module sum 8397\u21927592 (-805). Largest ON drops: layer1.py 5077\u21924284 (-793), pipeline.py 922\u2192910 (-12).",
      "reason": "Make membership dispatch decide from the emitted container value rather than pre-classifying source expressions, so CPython-backed needles can bridge into native list/tuple/dict contains while CPython containers still use __contains__. Preserve homogeneous tuple iteration element types. Add native dispatch for set.update(iterable) through the existing set spread lowering, and dict.pop(key, default) through py_dict_get/py_dict_del; single-argument dict.pop remains on the CPython path to preserve missing-key exception semantics."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-class-schema-and-byte-constants",
      "delta": "OFF multi 19763\u219219743 (-20), ON multi 2695\u21922648 (-47), ON per-module sum actual 7592\u21927571 (-21). Locked descending per-module entries: layer1.py ON 4284\u21924247 (-37), class_gen.py ON 519\u2192509 (-10), type_infer.py ON 658\u2192652 (-6); OFF layer1.py 19467\u219219453 (-14), class_gen.py 1157\u21921151 (-6), type_infer.py 658\u2192652 (-6).",
      "reason": "Add schema-bearing ClassType prepopulation for local and exported classes so pcc-Python annotations can express inheritance and fields instead of collapsing to DynType. Keep unresolved external class shells permissive so per-module self-compile still behaves like the old DynType path. Offset the new type-layer plumbing by removing CPython bytearray() from LLVM constant construction, replacing several reversed() uses in layer1 with pcc-native loops, and avoiding type(got).__name__ in the libpython-off type_infer stack. Conservative baseline update locks only the net total drops and per-module decreases; small structural increases in py_lift.py/pipeline.py remain governed by the existing ratchet instead of becoming new baselines."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-cross-module-class-dispatch",
      "delta": "OFF multi 19743\u219218597 (-1146), ON multi 2648\u21921493 (-1155). ON per-module sum was not recaptured because the new external-class registration helper adds 15 layer1.py fallback calls in independent per-module mode; the existing per-module ratchet still covers that cost instead of locking it in.",
      "reason": "Resolve unique exported ClassType annotations across modules, type method self as the enclosing class, and add positive-branch isinstance(name, ClassType) narrowing through simple 'and' conditions. Class-typed receivers can now register one matching external class and dispatch methods natively instead of routing through py_cpy_getattr/py_cpy_call. This is the flow-aware dispatch side of Insight 3: narrowing only pays off once the narrowed class value reaches a native method sink."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-str-split-maxsplit",
      "delta": "OFF multi 18597\u219218469 (-128), ON multi 1493\u21921319 (-174), ON per-module sum 7571/7586\u21927360 (-211 from the pre-fix actual). Locked descending per-module entries: layer1.py ON 4247\u21924138, pipeline.py ON 910\u2192820; layer1.py OFF 19453\u219219386, pipeline.py OFF 910\u2192820. runtime_abi.py OFF rises 1152\u21921160 from the new ABI declaration and remains governed by the existing ratchet rather than being recaptured upward.",
      "reason": "Add native py_str_split_maxsplit(s, sep, maxsplit) in the C runtime and pcc-Python runtime port, and dispatch str.split(sep, maxsplit) directly from codegen. This removes CPython split/getitem chains from module-name and option parsing code such as split('.', 1), split('=', 1), and split(None, 1), while preserving Python's maxsplit semantics for explicit separators and whitespace splitting."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-cpy-str-receiver-bridge",
      "delta": "OFF multi 18469\u219218439 (-30), ON multi 1319\u21921269 (-50), ON per-module sum 7360\u21927310 (-50). Locked descending per-module entry: pipeline.py OFF/ON 820\u2192770. layer1.py and py_lift.py per-module counts rise under the existing ratchet because the shared bridge logic lives there, so their old lower baselines remain in force.",
      "reason": "When a CPython-returned value feeds an already-native str method such as lower(), strip(), split(), or endswith(), bridge the receiver through py_cpy_to_pcc_obj and keep the rest of the string method chain on py_str_* helpers. This cuts chain-of-CPython amplification for subprocess/platform/listdir string results without adding another restricted source rewrite."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-native-file-open",
      "delta": "OFF multi 18439\u219218283 (-156), ON multi 1269\u21921039 (-230), ON per-module sum 7310\u21927091 (-219). Locked descending per-module entries: pipeline.py OFF/ON 770\u2192559, layer1.py ON 4138\u21924130. layer1.py OFF and runtime_abi.py OFF rise under the existing ratchet because the native file-object code and ABI declarations live there, so their old lower baselines remain in force.",
      "reason": "Add a native text-file runtime object and lower open(path, mode?, encoding=...) plus with-open read()/write()/close() through py_file_open/read_all/write/close. This removes the open/read/write/__enter__/__exit__ CPython chain from the pipeline's source/IR file reads and writes while keeping the standard with open(...) Python idiom."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-bridge-aware-ratchet",
      "delta": "ON multi 1039\u2192505 (-534), split as 18 bridge calls and 487 non-bridge py_cpy_* calls. ON per-module sum 7071\u21926462 (-609). Locked descending per-module entries: layer1.py 4130\u21923680, pipeline.py 559\u2192508, class_gen.py 509\u2192406, marshal.py 27\u219225, runtime_abi.py 3\u21920. OFF pipeline.py also drops 559\u2192508; OFF aggregate remains governed by the prior lower total ratchet.",
      "reason": "Recognize owner/alias IRBuilder receivers, replace remaining dataclass reflection in layer1.py with direct dataclass metadata access, treat pcc.llvm_capi.compat as an ON-only scaffold, add native value-position zip() and next(genexpr, default), and bridge CPython scalar equality into native py_obj_eq. Add bridge-aware ON ratchets so temporary py_cpy_to_pcc_* bridge calls cannot mask regressions in the original CPython fallback surface."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-utf8-ord-and-static-internals",
      "delta": "ON multi 505\u2192411 (-94), with bridge calls unchanged at 18 and non-bridge py_cpy_* calls 487\u2192393 (-94). ON per-module sum 6462\u21926382 (-80). Locked descending per-module entries: layer1.py 3680\u21923615 and pipeline.py 508\u2192493.",
      "reason": "Add native py_str_ord in both runtime tiers and lower ord(str) through it, so Unicode ord() no longer reads only the first UTF-8 byte. Replace internal str.encode() byte construction in codegen/class globals with a pcc-native UTF-8 encoder, remove regex use from IR libpython detection, avoid reverse/reversed/delattr dynamic calls in hot compiler internals, and make the builtin-name table static instead of importing builtins and calling dir()."
