    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-native-platform-machine",
      "delta": "ON multi 411\u2192400 (-11), bridge calls 18\u219216 (-2), non-bridge py_cpy_* calls 393\u2192384 (-9). ON per-module sum 6382\u21926371 (-11). Locked descending per-module entry: pipeline.py 493\u2192482.",
      "reason": "Treat platform as a native builtin module for import analysis and lower platform.machine() to py_platform_machine_str in the C-only substrate shared by both runtime archives. This removes the CPython platform.machine call and the follow-on cpy\u2192pcc string bridge while preserving the normal platform.machine().lower()/split() source idiom."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-native-subprocess-check-output",
      "delta": "ON multi 400\u2192383 (-17), bridge calls 16\u219213 (-3), non-bridge py_cpy_* calls 384\u2192370 (-14). ON per-module sum 6371\u21926362 (-9). Locked descending per-module entry: pipeline.py 482\u2192465; layer1.py rises 3615\u21923623 from the new native dispatch helper and remains governed by the existing lower ratchet.",
      "reason": "Add py_subprocess_check_output in a C-only process substrate object that survives the pcc-Python runtime archive replacement, and lower subprocess.check_output(argv, text=True|universal_newlines=True) natively. The bootstrap pipeline's command-output probes now return pcc strings directly, so downstream strip()/split() chains no longer need CPython call sites or cpy\u2192pcc string bridges. Unsupported bytes/encoding forms stay on the CPython fallback path."
    },
    {
