    {
      "date": "2026-04-28-native-process-stdlib-followup",
      "delta": "OFF multi 18283\u219217135 (-1148) and ON multi 322\u2192286 (-36), with ON bridge calls 10\u21929 (-1) and ON non-bridge py_cpy_* calls 312\u2192277 (-35). ON per-module actual sum 6315\u21926279 (-36). Locked descending per-module entries: pipeline.py OFF/ON 508/404\u2192368 and runtime_abi.py OFF 1152\u21920; layer1.py remains governed by its existing lower ratchet.",
      "reason": "Add native shutil.which(name), shlex.split(text), sys.executable, and bool-expression capture_output support for statement-only subprocess.run. This removes the CPython shutil/shlex/process-call edges from _resolve_pcc_binary, _append_libpython_link_flags, and _ensure_runtime, and lets os.path.dirname(sys.executable) stay on the native os.path path instead of bridging back from CPython. Treat pcc.llvm_capi.compat as a scaffold import for runtime_abi.py in both modes, since that module only needs IR type constructors; this offsets new ABI table entries by deleting the old OFF-mode compat CPython import surface instead of raising the ratchet."
    },
